---
description: Entity/master dropdowns must support type-to-narrow search (LocalSearchSelect or RemoteSearchSelect)
globs: frontend/src/**/*.{tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Searchable entity dropdowns

When the user picks a **master or entity** (ledger, account group, customer, vendor, item, style, order,
warehouse, department, designation, section, sewing line, cost center, employee, …), do **not** use a
native `<select>`. Native selects only jump by prefix and feel like one-letter search.

## Use one of these

1. **`RemoteSearchSelect`** (`frontend/src/components/app/RemoteSearchSelect.tsx`) — large lists with
   server search. Prefer helpers in `frontend/src/lib/remoteSelectFetchers.ts`
   (`fetchCustomerPage`, `fetchInventoryItemPage`, `fetchChartAccountPage`, `fetchStylePage`, …).
2. **`LocalSearchSelect`** (`frontend/src/components/app/LocalSearchSelect.tsx`) — lists already loaded
   in the page (warehouses, account groups, departments, designations, sewing lines, …).
   Filter is case-insensitive **contains** on the label (typing `operator` keeps “Junior Operator”
   and “Senior Operator”).

Shared wrappers that already type-to-narrow: `QuickAddSelect`, HR/Phase2 `SelectField` with
`searchable`, `HrEmployeeSelect`.

## Keep native `<select>` only for tiny enums

Yes/No, status (Draft/Active/…), debit/credit, financial year, currency, page size, gender, shipping
term, and similar fixed lists of a few options.

## Checklist for new pickers

- [ ] Entity list → Local or Remote search select (not native `<select>`).
- [ ] `required` / red required border still work when the form needs them.
- [ ] Inside tables or drawers, set `menuPortal` so the menu is not clipped.
- [ ] Update tests that used `selectOptions` to drive the combobox instead.
